    <item>
      <title>Connection - Walkthrough</title>
      <link>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/vulnyx/connection/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/vulnyx/connection/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;VulNyx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Difficulty&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;Hard&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OS&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;Windows&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attacker IP:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.10.10.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Machine IP:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.10.10.12&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The objective was to enumerate the target, identify the LFI vulnerability, recover the Administrator&amp;rsquo;s credentials, and obtain Administrator access through WinRM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;enumeration&#34;&gt;Enumeration&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;port-scanning&#34;&gt;Port Scanning&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I started with RustScan to identify exposed ports and running services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;rustscan -a 10.10.10.12 -b &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;500&lt;/span&gt; -- -sC -sV -A -oN nmap/init
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;results&#34;&gt;Results&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;PORT      STATE SERVICE       REASON  VERSION
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;80/tcp    open  http          syn-ack Apache httpd 2.4.58 ((Win64) OpenSSL/3.1.3 PHP/8.2.12)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;135/tcp   open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;139/tcp   open  netbios-ssn   syn-ack Microsoft Windows netbios-ssn
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;445/tcp   open  microsoft-ds? syn-ack
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;5985/tcp  open  http          syn-ack Microsoft HTTPAPI httpd 2.0 (SSDP/UPnP)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;47001/tcp open  http          syn-ack Microsoft HTTPAPI httpd 2.0 (SSDP/UPnP)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49664/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49665/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49666/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49667/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49668/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49669/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;49670/tcp open  msrpc         syn-ack Microsoft Windows RPC
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The scan revealed several interesting services:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Printer - Walkthrough</title>
      <link>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/hmv/printer/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/hmv/printer/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attacker IP:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.10.10.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Machine IP:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.10.10.22&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The objective was to enumerate the target, identify exposed services, gain initial access through an exposed NFS share, and escalate privileges by abusing an insecure log archiving script.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://nvru.github.io/images/hmv/printer/vm.png&#34; alt=&#34;Machine information&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;enumeration&#34;&gt;Enumeration&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;port-scanning&#34;&gt;Port Scanning&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;rustscan&#34;&gt;RustScan&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;rustscan -a 10.10.10.22 -- -sC -sV -A -oA nmap/rust
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;results&#34;&gt;Results&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;PORT      STATE SERVICE  VERSION
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;22/tcp    open  ssh      OpenSSH 8.4p1 Debian
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;111/tcp   open  rpcbind
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;2049/tcp  open  nfs_acl
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;38975/tcp open  nlockmgr
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;39487/tcp open  mountd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;48189/tcp open  mountd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;52073/tcp open  mountd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The scan showed SSH was available on port &lt;strong&gt;22&lt;/strong&gt; and an exposed &lt;strong&gt;NFS&lt;/strong&gt; service on &lt;strong&gt;2049&lt;/strong&gt;, making NFS the most interesting attack surface.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
